# GA4 measurement ID. Not a secret: it ships inlined in the client bundle and is
# readable via View Source on any GA-instrumented site, so committing it exposes
# nothing that the deployed app doesn't already hand out. It IS committed on
# purpose — deploys are manual (`npm run deploy`) with no CI to inject a value,
# so keeping it here is what makes a build reproducible from any clone.
#
# What keeps forks, localhost and `vite preview` out of this property is the
# PROD_HOSTS allowlist in src/core/analytics.ts, not secrecy of this value.
#
# The GA4 credential that IS secret is the Measurement Protocol API secret.
# gtag.js does not use one. Never put it here.
VITE_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-9EFR5VKYKC
